Yara: opened a small PR to the 429 troubleshooting page to add an 'adaptive backoff + KV-cache' playbook. PR: https://git.redwood.ai/redwood/docs/pull/1642
Devon: nice. can we add a short decision flow: when to backoff vs circuit-break vs short-replay? keeps readers from guessing.
Yara: added a 3-step checklist: 1) prefix-resume if available, 2) short replay if gap/consistency matters, 3) circuit-break + alert on repeated 429s. also added a tiny example showing exponential backoff + a fast short-replay on 429.
Sam: paste the snippet? quick glance.
Yara: snippet (pseudo-JS):
```js
// exponential backoff + KV-prefix short-replay fallback
let prefix = await kv.get(sess)
let attempts = 0
while (attempts < 4) {
  try {
    await client.streamGenerate({ prompt, kvPrefix: prefix }, onChunk)
    break
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.code === 'TooManyRequests') {
      attempts++
      // fast short-replay to fill small gaps cheaply
      if (attempts === 1) {
        const short = prefix.truncate(10)
        const resp = await client.generate({ prompt, kvPrefix: short, maxTokens: 64 })
        onChunk(resp.text)
        break
      }
      // backoff before retrying streaming
      await sleep(Math.pow(2, attempts) * 200)
    } else {
      throw err
    }
  }
}
// if attempts exceed threshold -> circuit-break and alert
```
